.. _communicator.ble.activate:

activate
~~~~~~~~

This event is shared from the parent machine.



This event is handled identically in all states.



These states handle this event:

* :ref:`initial <communicator.ble.initial>`
* :ref:`waiting <communicator.ble.waiting>`
* :ref:`scanning <communicator.ble.scanning>`
* :ref:`waiting_for_connection_window <communicator.ble.waiting_for_connection_window>`


This yields a state density of 100%.



No actions are taken in response to this event.



This event has data.

Translator: grab_parent_data_ptrs.

.. _communicator.ble.ble_comm:

ble_comm
~~~~~~~~

This event is shared from the parent machine.



This event has data.

Translator: translate_ble_comm.

The translator completely consumes the input event, which is thus never seen by the rest of the FSM.

